# Founder Idea Check: environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` in the repository root and fill in the values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored and is the only env file the app, the database tools and the evals read. Never commit
# it. Every secret below is blank on purpose.
#
# To run locally you need three things: DATABASE_URL (the default already matches `docker compose up -d`),
# AUTH_SECRET and OPENAI_API_KEY. Everything else is optional. The app validates what it reads in
# apps/chat/lib/env-schema.ts, and `bun run dev:local` prints what is missing for the features switched on in
# apps/chat/chat.config.ts before it starts. A few variables are read only by the research sidecar
# (apps/research/app/config.py) and are marked; the ones Vercel sets for you are listed at the end.
#
# The sidecar container that `docker compose up -d` starts does not read this file: it is fixed to the two sources
# that need no key. To run more sources, a SearXNG, or persona simulation, run the sidecar from its virtualenv with
# this file loaded (README-DEV.md, "The research sidecar, in a container or a virtualenv").

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required to run locally
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres connection string. This default is the pgvector Postgres that `docker compose up -d` starts
# (container ic-pg, bound to 127.0.0.1:5433, user and password both "postgres"). The database needs the pgvector
# extension; the stock `postgres` image does not have it. Create the schema with `bun run db:migrate`.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5433/ideacheck

# Secret that signs session cookies. Generate one: `openssl rand -base64 32`
AUTH_SECRET=

# OpenAI API key (https://platform.openai.com/api-keys). `ai.gateway` in apps/chat/chat.config.ts is "openai", so
# every chat turn, the phase gate's judge, fact extraction, titles, deep research and fact embeddings call OpenAI
# with this key, and you pay OpenAI for them. Without a key the app starts but cannot answer.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This deployment's public URL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Full URL including https://, exactly as the browser shows it. Auth trusts only this origin (plus the Vercel ones
# at the end), so a mismatch makes sign-out and every cookie-bearing POST fail with 403 INVALID_ORIGIN.
# `bun run dev:local` sets it to http://localhost:$PORT for you, so leave it unset locally (and browse to
# `localhost`, not 127.0.0.1). Required in production outside Vercel.
# APP_URL=https://example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research sidecar (optional; without it research is unavailable and the app says so)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The app finds the sidecar at `ai.tools.deepResearch.researchSidecarUrl` in apps/chat/chat.config.ts
# (http://localhost:8099), not through an environment variable. `curl http://127.0.0.1:8099/v1/health` shows which
# sources it will run and why any are off.

# Comma-separated source ids the operator turns on. Read by BOTH the app and the sidecar, so set it where both see
# it. Unset means "hackernews,web-keyless", the two sources that need no key. Known ids: hackernews, web-keyless,
# github, arctic-shift. An unknown id is refused and reported at /v1/health, never silently dropped.
# RESEARCH_ENABLED_SOURCES=hackernews,web-keyless

# A GitHub personal access token, for the `github` source. Without one that source is refused, because the
# keyless rate limit is used up by a single research run. Read by the app and the sidecar.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Base URL of a SearXNG instance you run, used by the `web-keyless` source. Without it that source asks
# DuckDuckGo's HTML endpoint alone, which many networks answer with a challenge page. Read by the sidecar only.
# The opt-in overlay starts one: `docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.searxng.yml up -d searxng`
# RESEARCH_SEARXNG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888

# "true" or "false". Read by the sidecar only; unset means hosted, the restrictive answer. The app takes the same
# answer from `ai.tools.deepResearch.hosted` in apps/chat/chat.config.ts, which is `false` for local use. Do not
# copy that setting into a deployment that serves other people.
# RESEARCH_HOSTED=false

# Persona simulation (OASIS) runs inside the sidecar and needs the heavy `simulation` build, not the default
# container. All read by the sidecar only; the sidecar also reads OPENAI_API_KEY from above.
# RESEARCH_SIM_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# RESEARCH_SIM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# RESEARCH_SIM_CONCURRENCY=8
# Reasoning effort sent with every simulated-agent call. Unset: the sidecar picks one that suits the model. Set to
# an empty value: none is sent. Anything else is sent as written.
# RESEARCH_SIM_REASONING_EFFORT=low

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redis (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Lets a streaming answer resume after a page reload. `docker compose up -d` starts a Valkey (a Redis-compatible
# server) on this port. Leave it unset unless that container is running: when it is set, the chat route connects
# to it as it loads and fails if it cannot.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6380

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign-in providers (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All three are off in apps/chat/chat.config.ts (`authentication.*`). Locally you sign in at /api/dev-login, which
# exists only in development. To use a provider, set its pair here and switch it on in chat.config.ts.

# GitHub OAuth app: https://github.com/settings/developers
# AUTH_GITHUB_ID=
# AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET=

# Google OAuth client: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=

# Sign in with Vercel: https://vercel.com/docs/sign-in-with-vercel
# VERCEL_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# VERCEL_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other model gateways (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if you change `ai.gateway` in apps/chat/chat.config.ts. The model ids in that file are typed per
# gateway, and `bun run fetch:models` refreshes the fallback model list for the gateway you pick.

# Vercel AI Gateway (gateway "vercel"): an API key, or an OIDC token (Vercel sets that one on its own deployments)
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=

# OpenRouter (gateway "openrouter")
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Anthropic directly (gateway "anthropic"); the base URL is only for a compatible proxy
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (gateway "openai-compatible")
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=
# OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=

# LiteLLM proxy (gateway "litellm"); the key only if your proxy requires one
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=
# LITELLM_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Features that are switched off in apps/chat/chat.config.ts (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secret for the cleanup cron endpoint (app/api/cron/cleanup). The endpoint refuses every request while this is
# unset. Generate one: `openssl rand -base64 32`
# CRON_SECRET=

# Web search keys. Deep research uses them only when `researchSidecarUrl` in chat.config.ts is empty; the
# standalone web-search tool, which is off, uses them too.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# Encrypts stored MCP connector credentials (base64, 44 characters). MCP connectors are off.
# Generate one: `openssl rand -base64 32`
# MCP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Code-execution sandbox (off). Outside Vercel it needs a team, project and token; the runtime ids pick the
# interpreter images and default to node22 and a Python image. VERCEL_SANDBOX_RUNTIME is the old name for the
# Python one.
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
# VERCEL_SANDBOX_RUNTIME_PYTHON=
# VERCEL_SANDBOX_RUNTIME_JAVASCRIPT=
# VERCEL_SANDBOX_RUNTIME=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Declared in apps/chat/lib/env-schema.ts, but no code reads them today, so setting them changes nothing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research cost is bounded by the iteration, concurrency and step limits under `deepResearch` in chat.config.ts.
# The `maxInputTokensPerRun` setting next to them has no reader either.
# EXA_API_KEY=
# RESEARCH_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set by Vercel on its deployments. Leave unset anywhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERCEL_URL                      the deployment's own host name, used as the public URL when APP_URL is unset
# VERCEL_ENV                      production, preview or development; the database migrator runs only for production
# VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL   the project's production domain, used as the public URL for production deployments
